 "result": "```python\nfrom build123d import *\n\nOD = 25.0\nBORE = 12.7\nL = 10.0\nHOLE = 3.3\n\nwith BuildPart() as part:\n    Cylinder(OD / 2, L)\n    Cylinder(BORE / 2, L, mode=Mode.SUBTRACT)\n    # radial hole along +X, through one wall only (from outside to bore)\n    r_mid = (OD / 2 + BORE / 2) / 2\n    wall = OD / 2 - BORE / 2\n    with Locations(Location((r_mid, 0, 0), (0, 90, 0))):\n        Cylinder(HOLE / 2, wall + 2, mode=Mode.SUBTRACT)\n\nresult = part.part\nexport_step(result, \"out.step\")\n```\n\nWait\u2014the hole cylinder length of wall+2 centered at r_mid extends 1 mm beyond each side: outward past the OD (fine) and inward into the bore (empty, fine), so it cuts only one wall.",
